    <!-- H2: Wall-clock time vs. real elapsed time -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.1rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 18px;">
        Wall-clock time vs. real elapsed time: The daylight saving factor
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.05rem;">
        An essential technical concept in time measurement is the distinction between <strong style="color: var(--text);">wall-clock time</strong> and <strong style="color: var(--text);">actual elapsed physical time</strong>:
      </p>

      <ul style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; padding-left: 24px; margin: 12px 0;">
        <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Wall-Clock Time:</strong> The reading shown on clocks on the wall or on your phone screen. A clock advancing from 01:00 to 03:00 displays a difference of 2 clock hours.</li>
        <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Elapsed Physical Time:</strong> The true number of physical SI seconds elapsed during the interval.</li>
      </ul>

      <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.05rem;">
        On the vast majority of calendar days, wall-clock duration and elapsed time are identical. However, on the two nights each year when Daylight Saving Time (DST) changes, they diverge:
      </p>

      <div style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, var(--panel)); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
        <h3 style="margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--accent);">How DST Impacts Overnight Intervals:</h3>
        <p style="margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
          • <strong>Spring Forward (March):</strong> Clocks skip from 01:59:59 to 03:00:00. An overnight shift scheduled from 01:00 to 05:00 appears to span 4 wall-clock hours, but in physical reality only <strong>3 hours</strong> elapsed.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
          • <strong>Fall Back (November):</strong> Clocks repeat the hour between 01:00 and 02:00. A shift scheduled from 01:00 to 05:00 appears to span 4 wall-clock hours, but actually spans <strong>5 hours</strong> of physical labor.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.05rem;">
        <strong>Calculator Limitation Notice:</strong> This browser-based tool uses standard local Date arithmetic based on your device's browser time zone. It does not allow selecting arbitrary separate source and destination IANA time zones. If you need to convert times between different geographical time zones (such as coordinating meeting times across London and New York), use our <a href="/" style="color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;">GMT to EST Converter</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- H2: Days vs. hours — which calculator do you need? -->
